## Risk tier (Article 6): high-risk.
- Article 6(2) uses the categories listed in Annex III; Annex III(3)(d) describes systems intended to monitor and detect disallowed student behaviour during tests in educational or vocational training institutions. The code connects the system to this education category rather than the product-safety route in Article 6(1)(a). [Article 6(2); Article 6(1)(a); Annex III(3)(d)]
- Article 6(3), third subparagraph, addresses the absence of significant harm, including material influence on decision-making, and gives profiling of natural persons overriding significance. The code records that the derogation was not established. [Article 6(3), third subparagraph]
